    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1979-p9.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Writing both radicals as powers of \\(2\\) gives \\[ \\begin{aligned} 4^{\\frac{1}{3}}8^{\\frac{1}{4}} &=2^{\\frac{2}{3}}2^{\\frac{3}{4}}\\\\ &=2^{\\frac{17}{12}}\\\\ &=2\\sqrt[12]{2^5}\\\\ &=2\\sqrt[12]{32}. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
